<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A high VES* effectively reflects both accurate and low latency models</span>, ranking GPT-4o highest (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2. Big SQL Metrics Zoom In on Performance ‣ 4. Evaluation ‣ Both Ends Count! Just How Good are LLM Agents at Text-to-“Big SQL”?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). It also reveals nuances, such as Opus models’ gains from perfect accuracy despite elevated execution times. Normalizing execution times to the fastest model (GPT-4o) shows it leads across all stages, suggesting a clear split between “fast” and “slow” models.</p>
</div>
